## Feature-Based CLEAN Architecture Structure

Your Flutter applications should follow this directory structure for optimal organization:

```
lib/
├── core/                          // Core package
│   ├── commerce/                  // Feature module  
│   │   ├── domain/                // Domain layer
│   │   │   ├── models/            // Domain entities
│   │   │   │   └── order.dart     // Type aliases for GraphQL fragments
│   │   │   └── repositories/      // Repository interfaces
│   │   │       └── order_repository_interface.dart
│   │   ├── infrastructure/        // Infrastructure layer
│   │   │   └── repositories/      // Repository implementations
│   │   │       └── order_repository.dart
│   │   └── graphql/               // GraphQL queries/mutations
│   │       └── orders.graphql     // Source GraphQL
│   │       └── orders.graphql.dart // Generated code
│   └── common/                    // Common utilities & failures
├── features/                      // Application features
│   └── shop/                      // Shop feature
│       ├── providers/             // Riverpod providers
│       │   └── cart_provider.dart // AsyncNotifier providers
│       ├── screens/               // UI screens
│       │   ├── cart_screen.dart
│       │   └── product_screen.dart
│       └── widgets/               // Reusable widgets
│           └── product_card.dart
└── main.dart
```

Remember these key principles:
- Domain should never depend on infrastructure
- Use interfaces for repositories
- Define type aliases for GraphQL fragments in domain/models
- Keep state management (Riverpod) in the application layer, not the core package
- Use AsyncNotifier for all async operations with proper loading, error, and success states
- Always provide immediate visual feedback for user interactions